Equivalence Groups Found
└── Modbus protocol client for reading/writing holding registers over TCP
    ├── Candidates : pymodbus, modbus-tk, minimalmodbus
    ├── Used APIs  : ModbusTcpClient, connect, read_holding_registers, write_register, isError, registers
    ├── Pitfalls   : pymodbus returns response objects with .isError() and .registers; minimalmodbus raises exceptions on error and returns raw values 
    │   directly, requiring a different error-handling pattern; minimalmodbus is primarily designed for serial (RTU) communication; using it for TCP requires 
    │   additional wrapping or a different transport setup; modbus-tk uses a master.execute() call pattern with function codes rather than named methods like 
    │   read_holding_registers/write_register; unit/slave addressing parameter naming and semantics differ across libraries (unit= vs slaveaddress= vs slave=)
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── All three libraries implement the Modbus protocol and can read/write holding registers to a field device, making them functionally interchangeable at 
        the protocol level. The file's own docstring explicitly calls out minimalmodbus as an intended substitution target for pymodbus. modbus-tk also 
        supports a TCP master/client role comparable to pymodbus's ModbusTcpClient.

